<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=665" title="View the profile of Naithein">Naithein</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 116<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/44-knightman.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Rawr ?<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/laldayen@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="laldayen@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://edit.yahoo.com/config/send_webmesg?.target=naithein%40yahoo.com"><img src="http://opi.yahoo.com/online?u=naithein%40yahoo.com&amp;m=g&amp;t=0" alt="naithein@yahoo.com" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="aim:goim?screenname=PadisharrCreel&amp;message=Hi.+Are+you+there?"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/aim.gif" alt="PadisharrCreel" border="0" /></a><br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=665"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.xanga.com/naithein" title="Muh Xanga" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:laldayen@hotmail.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1281.msg12749#msg12749"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/question.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1281.msg12749#msg12749">Is it really all down hill from here?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> November 18, 2004, 10:52:55 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							This is a quote from a friend who&#039;s on mainly 24/7 :-P<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"> <br /><br />&nbsp;the game is crashing and burning as we speak<br /><br />guilds are parting, and soon they all will fall<br /><br />Ascents not the best anymore, had more than 20guilds split apart last month, etc<br /><br />ruination, conviction, FoT, ascent. all breaking up<br /><br />Hegemony doesn&#039;t even exist as a guild anymore<br /><br />yep. its a lot worse than youve heard<br /><br />i&#039;m sure they will get rid of rodcent and put everyone else on another server<br />you sas:<br />It was teh best game in the world for 3+ years, shame for it to end this way </div><br />I&#039;m not sure if all this is true, but with so many new MMORPGs being released, tis quite obvious that EQ is getting a major kick in the ass.<br /><br />So Im wondering what you all think; ill be here till the end, I know that. <br /><br />I gave up on WoW and Comp can&#039;t run EQ2. So I&#039;m happy here.<br /><br />*Salute Rodcet*
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Naithein, Level 56 Paladin<br />Naithien, Level 54 Druid<br />--------------------------------------------<br />Naithein, Half Elf Paladin - EQ2<br />Xiakle, Iksar Furry - EQ2
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12750"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=361" title="View the profile of Toastie">Toastie</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 43<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=361"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1281.msg12750#msg12750"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1281.msg12750#msg12750">Re: Is it really all down hill from here?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #1 on:</b> November 18, 2004, 11:44:38 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							EQ&#039;s been dead for awhile for me... I’ve continued to play / raid with my guild because of the friends I play with, and I’m sure that’s the case with a large portion of the current EQ player base.&nbsp; I wouldn’t credit the release of eq2 or wow for &#039;bringing it all to an end&#039; as many people will say... i honestly think that people are growing tired of the game after so long, and are simply using eq2 and wow as an excuse to not play eq anymore<br /><br /><br />From <a href="http://www.thesteelwarrior.org/forum/showthread.php?t=9778" target="_blank"> The Steel Warrior</a><br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">There&#039;s no doubt that the combination of EQ2 and WoW will take the biggest chunk out of EQ that has ever been taken out of it. That said, I think it&#039;s a little early to panic. Don&#039;t disband your guild because you have 30 people on raids for a week or two. I think that there will be plenty of people left in EQ. You will see some guild mergers and probably just about all big guilds recruiting, which will take a bite out of the smaller/lower level guilds. Some guilds are going to fold. Some of the people that are gone now will be back though. I&#039;m sure a lot are trying out the WoW open beta, but not all of them will buy it. A lot of people will play EQ2 for a week or two (or a month or two) and decide it&#039;s not for them and come back. Others plan to play both games, since EQ2 is supposed to be more casual, but are mostly playing EQ2 right now because it&#039;s new. Some of them are playing Half Life 2 and will be back when they beat it in a week. Some of them are gone for good.<br /><br />If I was an EQ1 guild leader right now I would be telling people to relax, go grind out some AA, work on their epics, get their spells, play Half Life 2, or whatever, and in a couple weeks we can evaluate what we have and decide where to go from there, but I think it would be premature to say that EQ is dead and all the guilds are going to go belly up.<br /><br />My guild has been averaging about 10-15 less per night than usual the last week or so. We are still killing our farm targets but are short numbers for progression raids. Recruiting is harder on test than most servers, but we&#039;ll see how it goes.</div><br />While I voted yes, EQ is all down hill from here, I agree with this person, that EQ&#039;s not dead just yet, and we&#039;re bound to see some of the people who&#039;ve gone recently return to the game.<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12752"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=879" title="View the profile of Yslane">Yslane</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 9<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.radiophile.net/ferretava.jpg" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								In time you will fear the awesome power of ferrets<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<a href="aim:goim?screenname=Yssiebabo&amp;message=Hi.+Are+you+there?"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/aim.gif" alt="Yssiebabo" border="0" /></a><br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=879"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.echoesineternity.org" title="Echoes In Eternity" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:yslane@echoesineternity.org"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1281.msg12752#msg12752"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1281.msg12752#msg12752">Re: Is it really all down hill from here?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> November 19, 2004, 04:14:44 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1281.msg12749#msg12749">Quote from: Naithein on November 18, 2004, 10:52:55 pm</a></div><div class="quote">This is a quote from a friend who&#039;s on mainly 24/7 :-P<br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"> <br />the game is crashing and burning as we speak<br />guilds are parting, and soon they all will fall<br />Ascents not the best anymore, had more than 20guilds split apart last month, etc<br />ruination, conviction, FoT, ascent. all breaking up<br />Hegemony doesn&#039;t even exist as a guild anymore<br />yep. its a lot worse than youve heard<br /></div></div><br />I think your friend is being a bit of a doomspeaker or chicken little (The Sky is Falling The Sky is Falling!).&nbsp; Yes, Ascent has been passed up by DA/EIE and yes, Hegemony has for the most part scattered, but it&#039;s folly to assume that 4 major guilds on the server are breaking up or folding when all of the aforementioned guilds are to my knowledge, still raiding and recruiting.&nbsp; There&#039;s no way to really know what&#039;s up with a guild unless you are in it.&nbsp; <br /><br />I will however agree that the game has gotten a considerable bit smaller - it&#039;s a shake up, the game will go on.&nbsp; This is SOE&#039;s cash cow, they&#039;ll keep it around for as long as it is profitable.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
