								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1281.msg12759#msg12759">Re: Is it really all down hill from here?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #6 on:</b> November 19, 2004, 12:21:27 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1281.msg12758#msg12758">Quote from: Revenos on November 19, 2004, 12:11:38 pm</a></div><div class="quote">It&#039;s not so much the loss of players at the end-game that is important, but the near-total-absence of players at the lower ends that is the problem. Have you tried to get a group together with you lower-level alt lately? Unless, EQ1 gets a tranfusion of new people to the game, it will die of natural causes.<br /></div><br />I think that has more to do with we have less entirely new players coming to the game as well as the fact that it&#039;s SO BLOODY EASY to make levels now.  When most characters being rolled up belong to people who already have some time invested into the game, they can load up with good gear from the get-go and get a little bit of PL here and there from friends.  Going at it that way you can make 65+ in under a month /played without even working at it.  I mean seriously, the new expansion released on a Tuesday and people were 70 by late Thursday?&nbsp; The server population is crunching almost entirely into 65+ however, it&#039;s been that way for a good long while.
						</td>
