							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1281.msg12759#msg12759">Quote from: Yslane on November 19, 2004, 12:21:27 pm</a></div><div class="quote">I think that has more to do with we have less entirely new players coming to the game as well as the fact that it&#039;s SO BLOODY EASY to make levels now.  <br /></div><br />Heh, people will never be satisfied.&nbsp; Many say that EQ leveling is too hard, that the level grind sucks.&nbsp; That&#039;s one of EQ2 and WoW&#039;s selling points, the leveling is easier.&nbsp; Leveling in EQ, while not as tough as it was years ago, is still harder than those 2 games.&nbsp; IMO people will get tired of those new games much quicker than they got tired of EQ.&nbsp; Compare original EQ (everyone was a newbie, low level content, patchwork armor, no real high-end game except Vox/Naggy, etc.) to today&#039;s EQ, they&#039;re completely different.&nbsp; Except that original EQ wouldn&#039;t have been nearly the same experience with the spoiler sites and power gamers and endgame-motivated players that exist today.&nbsp; <br /><br />Pretty graphics will only hold people so long.&nbsp; I can&#039;t guarantee people will come back to EQ, but I doubt that the new games have the staying power to maintain their playerbase.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
