								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1281.msg12793#msg12793">Re: Is it really all down hill from here?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #11 on:</b> November 23, 2004, 03:01:12 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I agree, EQlive isn&#039;t going anywhere. Until you start seeing servers merging I wouldn&#039;t be too worried. <br /><br />Hell, people still play UO.<br /><br />EQII is fun.. but it&#039;s not FUN!.. and agree, to really enjoy the eye candy you need a top end rig. <br /><br />I will say it&#039;s been tons of fun starting over again in a brand new world but I wouldn&#039;t be surprised to see (after the free EQII month expries) lots of players returning to Live at some point (myself included).<br /><br />Nothing compares to the raid content offered by EQlive.<br /><br />cheers&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/wiggle2.gif" alt="Wiggle" border="0" /><br /><br />
						</td>
