							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Two things . . .<br /><br />One, Sony doestnt care about EQ I anymore and havent since they saw the peaked interest with a new game launch in SWG.&nbsp; For proof, see the last 4 or 5 expansions with the exception of maybe PoP.&nbsp; The core design team was either really bored after year 1-3 of EQ&#039;s launch or left for other projects, inhouse or elsewhere.<br /><br />Two, EQ 2 as a whole (graphics, sound, playability, character balance, trade skilling, vastness, expansion capability, support, funding, concept, storyline, etc) blows EQ 1 away IMO.&nbsp; Its like saying you want to break our your Atari and play some football while someone else is playing X-Box or PS2&#039;s Maddens 2005.<br /><br />Its almost over.&nbsp; They have no plans to cancel EQ until every last paying member cancels their account, they are probably still breaking even on EQ 1 every month or making slight profits.&nbsp; I think they are only keeping EQ 1 for PR and Spin as to not completely alienate all EQ 1 players.&nbsp; They want that money too, in time, they will get it.<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/banghead2.gif" alt="banghead2" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Mendolok<br />Chanter of Chanters<br />1000 faces for 1000 Camps
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
